---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site, contact } from "@/data/siteConfig";
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Nothing about you is collected, except the specific things listed in this policy. No tracking, no profiling, no selling."
>
  <p>
    The short version: nothing about you is collected beyond what is explicitly written here.
    What follows is the complete list, in plain words.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>“This site”, “the site”</strong> — the website at {site.url}, including every page
      and file served from it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“I”, “me”, “the owner”</strong> — {site.fullName}, who runs this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“You”, “visitor”</strong> — anyone who visits the site or submits a form on it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Personal information”</strong> — information that identifies you or can be
      linked to you, such as a name, an email address, or a phone number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Forms”</strong> — the contact form and the review forms.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Review forms”</strong> — the feedback forms for written works published on this
      site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Host”</strong> — Cloudflare Pages, the service that delivers this site to your
      browser.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What this site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No analytics and no visitor statistics that identify you.</li>
    <li>No advertising, tracking pixels, or behavioural profiling.</li>
    <li>No cookies set by this site for tracking.</li>
    <li>No personal information is sold.</li>
    <li>
      No database of visitors. The only information that exists is what you deliberately
      submit through a form, and it is handled as described below.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What is processed to deliver a page</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Like any web host, Cloudflare
    processes standard technical request data in order to serve pages and keep the site
    online: your IP address, the page or file requested, the date and time, your browser and
    device type (user-agent), the page you came from, and an approximate location.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare uses this for normal operation and security — caching, bot protection, and
    defence against attacks. It is processed on Cloudflare's systems, under
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a
    >. I do not receive it as a readable record and I do not keep copies of it.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not use cookies of its own. The only thing it stores on your device is
    your light/dark theme preference, kept in your browser's local storage. That value stays
    in your browser and is never sent to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare may set its own security cookies (for example, to verify that a visitor is
    not a bot). Those cookies belong to Cloudflare and are governed by their policy above.
    Clearing site data in your browser removes the local theme setting.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    A few outside services are involved in showing this site. None of them are used for
    advertising or tracking, but each one receives your IP address as part of any normal web
    request:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> — hosting, caching, and security.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts</strong> — delivers the typefaces used on the site
      (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Google Privacy Policy</a
      >).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Web3Forms</strong> — only if you choose to submit one of the forms
      (<a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Web3Forms Privacy Policy</a
      >).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. The forms, and what they send</h2>
  <p>
    Forms are the only way this site receives anything from you, and using them is entirely
    voluntary. Both types are delivered through Web3Forms to my inbox, but they are treated
    differently.
  </p>

  <h3>(a) Contact form — private</h3>
  <p>
    The contact form asks for your name, an email address or phone number, and your message.
    It is used only to read your message and reply to you. What you send through it is not
    published, not shared, and not added to a mailing list. Please do not send passwords,
    financial details, identity documents, or anything else sensitive. Emailing me directly
    works the same way.
  </p>

  <h3>(b) Review forms — may be published</h3>
  <p>
    Review forms ask for your name (required), a star rating, what helped you, and any
    suggestions, plus an optional permission checkbox. A submitted review is not private.
    By submitting a review form, you agree that the content you submit may be used and shared
    for testimonial and marketing purposes — on this site or elsewhere, together with your
    name. Do not include anything you would not want published. If you do not agree to that,
    please email me instead:
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. What you control</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can use the entire site without submitting anything.</li>
    <li>You can block third-party requests (such as fonts) in your browser.</li>
    <li>You can clear cookies and local storage at any time.</li>
    <li>
      You can ask me to delete a contact message you have sent at any time by emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can ask me to take down a published review. Once a review has been shared, copies
      made elsewhere may stay outside my control.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. There is no
    hidden collection now, and any future change will be written here, not discovered later.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy on this site:
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
